WEBVTT

00:00:25.790 --> 00:00:28.700
"Original Manga by Kenta Shinohara
SHUEISHA JUMP COMICS"

00:00:44.830 --> 00:00:47.750
"Series Writer: Norimitsu Kaihou"
"Character Design: Keiko Kurosawa"

00:01:00.410 --> 00:01:03.250
"Audio Director: Satoki Iida"
"CGI: LARX ENTERTAINMENT"
"CG Director: Daisuke Katou"
"Music Masaru: Yokoyama, Hiroaki Nobusawa"

00:01:09.040 --> 00:01:12.200
No... The thrusters won't work...

00:01:15.200 --> 00:01:17.000
Everyone's gone...

00:01:18.870 --> 00:01:20.700
I'm scared...!

00:01:22.330 --> 00:01:25.250
"Animation Producer: Yuji Higa"
"Animation Production: Lerche Assistant"
"Director: Yusuke Shibata"
"Director: Masaomi Ando"

00:01:28.040 --> 00:01:29.830
I'm scared...

00:01:32.200 --> 00:01:35.620
Being all alone is terrifying...!

00:02:22.040 --> 00:02:26.000
"Aries' Apartment
Day before leaving for camp"

00:02:26.540 --> 00:02:28.120
Aries!

00:02:28.120 --> 00:02:30.290
Are you ready for tomorrow?

00:02:30.290 --> 00:02:33.290
Yep! Everything is perfectly packed!

00:02:33.290 --> 00:02:35.080
Hmm?

00:02:35.080 --> 00:02:36.000
What's this?

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:41.080
Whoa! My passport! I forgot to pack it!

00:02:41.080 --> 00:02:42.910
I'll ask just one more time...

00:02:42.910 --> 00:02:45.660
Aries, are you sure
you're ready for tomorrow?

00:02:45.660 --> 00:02:47.870
Uh, of course!

00:02:47.870 --> 00:02:51.120
How about you, Mom?
Will you be okay alone?

00:02:51.120 --> 00:02:53.950
I'm going to be gone
for five whole days...

00:02:56.410 --> 00:02:59.370
Don't worry, just enjoy yourself.

00:02:59.370 --> 00:03:02.330
Remind me, where is the camp site?

00:03:02.330 --> 00:03:04.540
It's Planet McPa!

00:03:10.790 --> 00:03:14.410
"Mousanish Spaceport
Day of departure"

00:03:15.120 --> 00:03:18.950
Flight 77 departing from Mousanish
will be leaving at 1430 hours...

00:03:18.950 --> 00:03:23.120
So excited...

00:03:23.120 --> 00:03:25.410
So excited...!

00:03:25.410 --> 00:03:27.160
Planet...

00:03:27.160 --> 00:03:29.080
...Camp!

00:03:29.620 --> 00:03:30.450
Oh?

00:03:30.450 --> 00:03:31.580
Whoa!

00:03:31.580 --> 00:03:33.040
I'm so sorry!

00:03:33.040 --> 00:03:36.370
You're quite excited,
aren't you, young lady?

00:03:36.370 --> 00:03:38.700
Oh, thank you!

00:03:38.700 --> 00:03:42.830
Planet Camp, did you say?
Are you from Caird High?

00:03:42.830 --> 00:03:43.790
Hmm?

00:03:43.790 --> 00:03:46.290
I went, too. A long time ago.

00:03:46.290 --> 00:03:50.160
Really? Was it Planet McPa?

00:03:50.160 --> 00:03:51.830
Yes.

00:03:51.830 --> 00:03:54.160
Five days, students only.

00:03:54.160 --> 00:03:58.540
It was my very first space trip,
so it was scary at first.

00:03:58.540 --> 00:04:01.790
But once I got to know the rest of my team,

00:04:01.790 --> 00:04:05.250
it was more fun than I could have imagined.

00:04:12.830 --> 00:04:17.620
Go enjoy yourself. But do be careful--
you seem a bit clumsy.

00:04:17.620 --> 00:04:21.080
Ha, ha... I'm not clumsy, sir.

00:04:21.080 --> 00:04:22.580
I'm a woman!

00:04:24.790 --> 00:04:26.160
--Huh?
--Huh?

00:04:29.660 --> 00:04:32.160
A thief, as if on cue!

00:04:32.160 --> 00:04:33.580
What?!

00:04:33.580 --> 00:04:35.160
Uh, umm...

00:04:35.160 --> 00:04:36.580
--Stop! Beef!

00:04:36.580 --> 00:04:38.500
--You mean "thief"!
--Stop! Beef!

00:04:41.790 --> 00:04:43.950
Huh? What an idiot.

00:04:43.950 --> 00:04:46.540
He can't catch up on foot...

00:04:46.540 --> 00:04:48.910
Oh, wow, he's fast!

00:04:55.370 --> 00:04:57.750
Oh, anti-gravity shoes!

00:04:57.750 --> 00:04:59.250
Take this!

00:04:59.250 --> 00:05:01.000
Un... Timut... Daibamomo!

00:05:01.000 --> 00:05:02.410
Say what?!

00:05:02.410 --> 00:05:03.790
Argh!

00:05:03.830 --> 00:05:06.290
"Untimut
Daibamomo!!"

00:05:09.160 --> 00:05:11.040
Oh, no, wait!

00:05:11.040 --> 00:05:14.000
I was trying to say, "Ultimate Dive Bomb."

00:05:14.000 --> 00:05:17.160
Dang, why did I have to come up
with such a mouthful of a move name...

00:05:17.160 --> 00:05:19.080
Are you okay?

00:05:20.620 --> 00:05:22.660
Here, your bag.

00:05:24.450 --> 00:05:28.620
Thank you very much.
You got it back for me.

00:05:30.660 --> 00:05:32.620
Mr. Untimut Daibamomo!

00:05:32.620 --> 00:05:34.250
That's not my name!

00:05:34.250 --> 00:05:36.500
Can that possibly be a person's name?!

00:05:36.500 --> 00:05:39.660
Also, who launches an attack
while screaming his own name?

00:05:39.660 --> 00:05:42.000
Thank you so very much!

00:05:42.000 --> 00:05:43.410
Seriously...

00:05:43.410 --> 00:05:44.580
Huh?

00:05:45.500 --> 00:05:47.330
Oh, patrol bots...

00:05:47.910 --> 00:05:51.330
Spaceport security sure is quick.

00:05:51.330 --> 00:05:53.620
This guy is a purse-snatcher.

00:05:53.620 --> 00:05:56.910
I knocked him out by accident.

00:05:57.950 --> 00:05:58.830
Huh?

00:05:58.830 --> 00:06:02.450
You are under arrest for assault.

00:06:02.450 --> 00:06:03.580
Huh?

00:06:05.370 --> 00:06:06.580
Wha...?

00:06:06.580 --> 00:06:08.750
Catch, and...!

00:06:08.750 --> 00:06:10.040
No!

00:06:10.040 --> 00:06:11.750
Go!

00:06:11.750 --> 00:06:13.370
One, two! One, two!

00:06:13.370 --> 00:06:16.200
Hey! Not me!

00:06:16.200 --> 00:06:20.080
Wait, please!

00:06:22.120 --> 00:06:30.500
Passengers boarding AQF flight 318 to Ikemir...

00:06:30.500 --> 00:06:34.660
...your flight will begin boarding at noon...

00:06:34.660 --> 00:06:37.450
Hey, are you going on the camp too?

00:06:41.450 --> 00:06:42.500
I'm sorry.

00:06:42.500 --> 00:06:44.790
What?! Sorry for what?!

00:06:48.790 --> 00:06:51.910
Hey there. Are you lost?

00:06:51.910 --> 00:06:54.580
No, I'm not lost.

00:06:54.580 --> 00:06:57.580
Oh. That's good. This area is...

00:07:01.120 --> 00:07:03.250
What are you doing?

00:07:03.250 --> 00:07:07.080
Calculating the trajectory
from here to Planet McPa.

00:07:07.080 --> 00:07:07.700
Quitterie...

00:07:07.700 --> 00:07:09.950
But why, though?

00:07:09.950 --> 00:07:11.410
Just for fun.

00:07:13.120 --> 00:07:15.870
Hmm? Oh, it's you.

00:07:15.870 --> 00:07:20.250
Stop fidgeting around. What do you want?

00:07:20.250 --> 00:07:22.830
It's... nothing.

00:07:26.950 --> 00:07:28.410
Can we go already?

00:07:28.410 --> 00:07:31.750
Just wait a bit longer.
I'll explain when everyone's here.

00:07:31.750 --> 00:07:34.330
You know we're past schedule, right?

00:07:34.330 --> 00:07:38.200
Fashionably late from the very beginning?
Quite a bold statement.

00:07:38.200 --> 00:07:39.870
Ugh.

00:07:39.870 --> 00:07:42.290
How rude, right?

00:07:42.290 --> 00:07:43.290
I'm sorry.

00:07:43.290 --> 00:07:45.120
Seriously, why?!

00:07:45.120 --> 00:07:46.790
I'm sorry!

00:07:49.580 --> 00:07:51.450
I'm late!

00:07:51.450 --> 00:07:53.120
Finally here, huh?

00:07:53.120 --> 00:07:55.160
Quiet. You are?

00:07:55.160 --> 00:07:58.250
Um, a beef got me, and he saved me,

00:07:58.250 --> 00:08:00.950
but he got one-two'ed, and...

00:08:00.950 --> 00:08:02.950
It really was a Ferris wheel!

00:08:02.950 --> 00:08:04.750
Catch a breath and make
some sense, please?!

00:08:04.750 --> 00:08:06.580
Name and class?

00:08:06.580 --> 00:08:07.790
Yes!

00:08:07.790 --> 00:08:11.330
Aries Spring, Class 2-B!

00:08:11.330 --> 00:08:15.750
I love poetry, and my special skill
is that I never forget people I meet.

00:08:15.750 --> 00:08:19.950
My personality is, uh...
People say I can't read the room.

00:08:19.950 --> 00:08:21.450
I really don't understand.

00:08:21.450 --> 00:08:25.000
I said name and class, not life story!
That's basic room reading!

00:08:25.000 --> 00:08:26.950
What's her deal?

00:08:26.950 --> 00:08:28.660
She's quite unique.

00:08:28.660 --> 00:08:30.290
Takes one to know one.

00:08:30.290 --> 00:08:34.450
Ahem. So, back on track.

00:08:34.450 --> 00:08:40.580
This is the day you've been waiting for,
Caird High, team B-5, Space Camp.

00:08:40.580 --> 00:08:46.450
We teachers will deliver you to Planet McPa,
then leave immediately after.

00:08:46.450 --> 00:08:52.790
The goal of the Planet Camp is to spend
five days on site, eight students only.

00:08:52.790 --> 00:08:55.830
The team was assembled randomly.

00:08:55.830 --> 00:08:58.910
Most of you must have met for the first time.

00:08:58.910 --> 00:09:02.250
Deepen your bond,
feel the vastness of space,

00:09:02.250 --> 00:09:04.830
and have a great experience.

00:09:04.830 --> 00:09:06.290
Also...

00:09:07.700 --> 00:09:11.660
She is Funicia Rafaeli, Quitterie's sister.

00:09:11.660 --> 00:09:15.000
She will be joining you on this camp.

00:09:16.950 --> 00:09:21.080
Each team is assigned a special task.

00:09:21.080 --> 00:09:25.540
In your case, bringing along
a ten-year-old is the task.

00:09:25.540 --> 00:09:31.120
So we asked Quitterie to bring her sister.

00:09:31.120 --> 00:09:33.910
Come on, say hi.

00:09:33.910 --> 00:09:40.250
I'm Funicia, I'm ten years old.
I'm sorry to cause you trouble.

00:09:40.250 --> 00:09:43.750
Are you sure it's safe to take this kid along?

00:09:43.750 --> 00:09:46.700
I'm really uncomfortable around kids.

00:09:46.700 --> 00:09:49.000
I, I...

00:09:50.370 --> 00:09:54.330
You wanna piece of me, you little brat?!

00:09:54.330 --> 00:09:55.660
What?!

00:09:55.660 --> 00:09:57.120
Funicia!

00:09:57.120 --> 00:09:59.500
That was Beego.

00:09:59.500 --> 00:10:01.160
Impressive.

00:10:01.160 --> 00:10:05.370
It's a puppet that automatically conveys
thoughts into a cartoon character's voice.

00:10:05.370 --> 00:10:11.120
Ahem! Anyway, so this team
will have one additional member.

00:10:11.120 --> 00:10:12.410
Hey, Mom!

00:10:12.410 --> 00:10:13.700
I'm your teacher!

00:10:13.700 --> 00:10:18.580
Teacher, we already have
exactly eight people.

00:10:18.580 --> 00:10:21.250
Yes, we're missing one more.

00:10:21.250 --> 00:10:24.790
We may have to leave him behind.

00:10:24.790 --> 00:10:26.910
Too close, too close.

00:10:26.910 --> 00:10:30.580
Getting left behind for being late?
Not cool at all.

00:10:31.080 --> 00:10:32.290
"Tadah!"
--One, two! One, two!

00:10:32.290 --> 00:10:34.660
"Tadah!"
--You really are uncool!
--One, two! One, two!

00:10:34.660 --> 00:10:36.870
Are you a participant?

00:10:36.870 --> 00:10:39.200
Finally, the misunderstanding is over!

00:10:42.040 --> 00:10:45.830
Kanata Hoshijima. I'm your captain!

00:10:45.830 --> 00:10:48.080
Follow me, everyone!

00:10:48.080 --> 00:10:50.870
Let's go, to Planet McPa!

00:10:53.330 --> 00:10:57.450
Hmm? I thought we vote
to choose a captain.

00:10:57.450 --> 00:11:02.660
Yeah, so I thought I might declare
my candidacy early...

00:11:02.660 --> 00:11:06.040
What's wrong with this guy?!
He should be sorry, not bossy!

00:11:06.040 --> 00:11:09.870
Terrible first impressions.
You're not getting our votes.

00:11:09.870 --> 00:11:11.910
What? For real?

00:11:11.910 --> 00:11:13.660
Retreat, retreat...

00:11:13.660 --> 00:11:16.950
Someone needs to check his ego.

00:11:16.950 --> 00:11:19.290
But I guess that's the beauty of youth.

00:11:19.290 --> 00:11:22.120
Why does this puppet sound so elderly?

00:11:25.660 --> 00:11:30.660
"Caird High Space Ship
Ready for departure"

00:11:41.040 --> 00:11:45.790
That pink and black suit, it's from SMB, right?

00:11:45.790 --> 00:11:47.370
Same as Funi!

00:11:47.370 --> 00:11:48.370
Yep!

00:11:48.370 --> 00:11:54.540
I don't have siblings,
so I'm jealous of sisters who are close.

00:11:54.540 --> 00:11:56.750
It's not like that.

00:12:01.950 --> 00:12:06.080
Funi, I love your little skirt!

00:12:08.540 --> 00:12:12.200
Yunhua, your suit is by Hyperion!

00:12:12.200 --> 00:12:15.580
Same as mine!

00:12:15.580 --> 00:12:16.910
Yes.

00:12:20.870 --> 00:12:24.620
Whoa... Awesome!

00:12:24.620 --> 00:12:27.330
He is interesting.

00:12:27.330 --> 00:12:33.910
His declaration to run.
Is it that desirable, to become captain?

00:12:33.910 --> 00:12:35.790
--It is a big responsibility.
--Out of my way.

00:12:35.790 --> 00:12:38.950
--He'd have to round everyone up.
--Sorry.

00:12:40.410 --> 00:12:41.910
What are you talking about?

00:12:41.910 --> 00:12:44.950
Who should be captain.

00:12:44.950 --> 00:12:47.660
Yes! Me! I've volunteered!

00:12:47.660 --> 00:12:51.620
Calm down. That's why you
didn't get chosen.

00:12:51.620 --> 00:12:54.120
Past tense?! How?!

00:12:54.120 --> 00:12:55.330
Excuse me.

00:12:55.330 --> 00:12:57.290
Oh, sorry.

00:12:57.290 --> 00:12:59.330
It's pretty much settled.

00:12:59.330 --> 00:13:03.830
Who knows where you'll lead us
off to if you became captain.

00:13:03.830 --> 00:13:05.830
What?!

00:13:05.830 --> 00:13:08.750
Wandering off sounds like fun.

00:13:08.750 --> 00:13:12.000
You mean getting lost.

00:13:12.000 --> 00:13:13.250
--Okay, we're taking off.
Fasten your seatbelts.

00:13:13.250 --> 00:13:15.250
--I'm ready.
--Okay, we're taking off.
Fasten your seatbelts.

00:13:16.160 --> 00:13:17.830
Did something happen?

00:13:17.830 --> 00:13:19.450
How should I know.

00:13:20.450 --> 00:13:24.000
I recently transferred to this school.

00:13:24.000 --> 00:13:26.080
No wonder you seemed unfamiliar.

00:13:26.080 --> 00:13:29.120
Yes! It's only been about a month.

00:13:29.120 --> 00:13:32.040
Pleas be my friend, Quitterie!

00:13:33.910 --> 00:13:40.040
I'm only here for the credits.
Not to socialize.

00:13:41.910 --> 00:13:43.790
I...

00:13:43.790 --> 00:13:47.040
I want to be friends with everyone.

00:13:48.660 --> 00:13:52.290
She doesn't listen, does she?

00:13:54.330 --> 00:13:57.000
I'm so excited for this camp!

00:14:03.000 --> 00:14:05.580
Increase output to Ether engines.

00:14:05.580 --> 00:14:08.160
Deploy Cleaving Field.

00:14:08.160 --> 00:14:12.000
Transition to acceleration-expansion phase.
Begin Cleaving.

00:14:19.580 --> 00:14:22.160
We've entered faster-than-light travel.

00:14:22.160 --> 00:14:24.950
You can deactivate your helmets and relax.

00:14:24.950 --> 00:14:30.120
Wow, it's stuffy in here.
Can I open the windows?

00:14:30.120 --> 00:14:34.250
Four hours is a lot.
Isn't there a TV or something?

00:14:34.250 --> 00:14:36.250
Is there a shower on this ship?

00:14:36.250 --> 00:14:40.200
Sir, I can't relax without
changing into my gown.

00:14:40.200 --> 00:14:42.660
I said relax, not lose all control!

00:14:51.950 --> 00:14:55.080
I've finally come this far...

00:14:55.080 --> 00:14:56.450
Teacher...

00:15:03.450 --> 00:15:07.330
Teacher, I'm not going to space anymore.

00:15:08.330 --> 00:15:14.450
Track and field is best for me.
I want to focus on it.

00:15:14.450 --> 00:15:16.080
Is it your Dad?

00:15:18.080 --> 00:15:22.250
Life in sports is wonderful, too.

00:15:22.250 --> 00:15:27.450
But you're much too young to lock in
what's best for you and what's not.

00:15:27.450 --> 00:15:31.120
Then how do I know what to do?

00:15:31.120 --> 00:15:33.620
Based on what you like, of course.

00:15:35.160 --> 00:15:40.120
Teacher, you really think life is that easy?

00:15:40.120 --> 00:15:41.580
I really do.

00:15:42.410 --> 00:15:47.870
You can reach the skies, and beyond.

00:15:50.500 --> 00:15:51.950
Really?

00:15:53.330 --> 00:15:57.830
Yes, and my purpose is
to help you do just that.

00:16:02.910 --> 00:16:04.500
Wow...

00:16:09.870 --> 00:16:11.120
Excuse me!

00:16:13.200 --> 00:16:16.330
Thank you for helping me at the space port!

00:16:16.330 --> 00:16:18.700
Hey, Aries Spring.

00:16:18.700 --> 00:16:20.410
Didn't know you were on the same team!

00:16:20.410 --> 00:16:23.700
Oh, wow, you learned my name already!

00:16:23.700 --> 00:16:25.660
Thank you very much!

00:16:25.660 --> 00:16:27.870
Uh... Kanata...

00:16:27.870 --> 00:16:29.450
Something Daibamomo!

00:16:29.450 --> 00:16:31.910
You need to learn my name, too!

00:16:31.910 --> 00:16:36.040
I had my wallet in this bag.
I can't thank you enough..

00:16:36.040 --> 00:16:39.080
As a token of my gratitude...

00:16:39.080 --> 00:16:41.120
Nah, don't mention it.

00:16:41.120 --> 00:16:43.750
Would you like a frozen tangerine?

00:16:43.750 --> 00:16:45.410
What are you, my grandma?!

00:16:48.410 --> 00:16:51.200
I was really impressed

00:16:51.200 --> 00:16:54.160
that you volunteered to become champion.

00:16:54.160 --> 00:16:56.410
You mean captain.

00:16:56.410 --> 00:16:59.870
Why did you, though?

00:16:59.870 --> 00:17:04.330
I want to be an explorer of space.

00:17:04.330 --> 00:17:08.950
I want to own a ship,
and go to an uncharted star.

00:17:08.950 --> 00:17:12.910
I thought being captain here
would be a great first step.

00:17:12.910 --> 00:17:14.500
Wow.

00:17:14.500 --> 00:17:19.450
Impressive! You have such
solid dreams already.

00:17:19.450 --> 00:17:24.450
It's actually my mentor's dream.

00:17:24.450 --> 00:17:29.080
He passed away in an accident.

00:17:29.080 --> 00:17:31.910
I don't know if I can say
I'm inheriting his wishes,

00:17:31.910 --> 00:17:36.080
but that's where it all started.

00:17:41.040 --> 00:17:44.160
I'm sure you'll achieve it! I'm so impressed!

00:17:44.160 --> 00:17:47.660
Whoa, okay, wow you're passionate...

00:17:47.660 --> 00:17:50.290
Would you like some iced tea?

00:17:50.290 --> 00:17:52.080
What are you, my grandma?!

00:18:00.040 --> 00:18:05.000
"Planet McPa
Camp destination"

00:18:09.290 --> 00:18:11.200
Atmosphere check.

00:18:11.200 --> 00:18:13.160
Content, pressure, clear.

00:18:13.160 --> 00:18:14.660
Students.

00:18:14.660 --> 00:18:17.040
We've arrived at Planet McPa!

00:18:17.040 --> 00:18:19.040
Hooray!

00:18:20.000 --> 00:18:22.660
Take your belongings and enter the airlock.

00:18:22.660 --> 00:18:27.750
Once everyone's off the ship,
we will head home.

00:18:27.750 --> 00:18:30.750
We'll be back for you in five days.

00:18:32.000 --> 00:18:33.750
Wow...

00:18:36.120 --> 00:18:38.080
This is McPa...

00:18:38.080 --> 00:18:40.790
It's not like the view from the ship.

00:18:40.790 --> 00:18:42.200
Look at the clouds.

00:18:42.200 --> 00:18:46.120
Those were clouds? They looked like lakes.

00:18:46.120 --> 00:18:49.870
We're really in a different planet...

00:18:59.200 --> 00:19:01.120
Okay then.

00:19:01.120 --> 00:19:04.580
Let's get to the lodge,
get out of our suits, and explore!

00:19:04.580 --> 00:19:08.040
Hey! Why are you bossing us around?!

00:19:08.040 --> 00:19:12.540
Follow me, everyone!
Who knows what we'll find here!

00:19:14.540 --> 00:19:16.500
Was that an explosion?!

00:19:18.370 --> 00:19:20.330
Does the ground explode on this planet?!

00:19:20.330 --> 00:19:24.500
No, that's just his anti-gravity unit.

00:19:24.500 --> 00:19:29.330
Oh, it must have been damaged
by the Ultimate Dive Bomb...

00:19:30.790 --> 00:19:33.910
Hey, what's that?

00:19:33.910 --> 00:19:36.830
Let's leave the idiot here
and get to the lodge.

00:19:36.830 --> 00:19:38.290
Hey, don't leave your captain behind.

00:19:38.290 --> 00:19:39.910
Who said you're captain?!

00:19:39.910 --> 00:19:43.120
Hey guys, what is that?

00:19:55.500 --> 00:19:57.250
What is that...?

00:20:00.200 --> 00:20:02.790
I've never seen anything like it.

00:20:06.200 --> 00:20:07.450
It's coming closer.

00:20:07.450 --> 00:20:09.040
Be careful, everyone!

00:20:09.040 --> 00:20:11.000
Hey, this is cool.

00:20:11.000 --> 00:20:12.330
Whoa, hey...

00:20:13.160 --> 00:20:14.910
Hey you, stop!

00:20:14.910 --> 00:20:16.950
What, are you scared?

00:20:16.950 --> 00:20:21.200
This is a foreign planet,
but it's still just a nature park.

00:20:21.200 --> 00:20:24.000
Obviously this is just theatrics.

00:20:41.040 --> 00:20:42.580
Everyone, run!

00:20:42.580 --> 00:20:45.540
If you've disabled your helmets,
put them back on!

00:21:24.830 --> 00:21:26.580
What's going on?

00:21:53.450 --> 00:21:55.250
You're safe.

00:21:56.750 --> 00:21:59.000
I'm pulling you up now.

00:21:59.000 --> 00:21:59.910
I can help!

00:21:59.910 --> 00:22:02.750
Okay, grab the other arm!

00:22:19.000 --> 00:22:21.750
Teacher! Hold on!

00:22:21.750 --> 00:22:23.370
I'll get a rope!

00:22:23.370 --> 00:22:25.450
No, it's too dangerous!

00:22:26.500 --> 00:22:31.660
Leave me, focus on saving yourselves.

00:22:31.660 --> 00:22:35.580
Help is coming.
You have to survive until then.

00:22:36.580 --> 00:22:39.700
When things seem hopeless...

00:22:39.700 --> 00:22:41.120
...act tough!

00:22:53.540 --> 00:22:57.160
What?! Why am I in space?!

00:23:07.250 --> 00:23:08.620
Is that...?

00:23:08.620 --> 00:23:10.830
Can someone hear me?

00:23:13.040 --> 00:23:14.750
Everyone...!

00:23:16.620 --> 00:23:18.330
Guys, can you hear me?

00:23:18.330 --> 00:23:20.910
Are your communicators working?

00:23:20.910 --> 00:23:22.290
Yes!

00:23:22.290 --> 00:23:25.950
What the heck is going on?!

00:23:25.950 --> 00:23:28.330
Why are we in space?!

00:23:28.330 --> 00:23:30.290
It's that sphere.

00:23:30.290 --> 00:23:33.200
It sucked us in, and now we're here.

00:23:33.200 --> 00:23:35.000
This is an emergency!

00:23:35.000 --> 00:23:37.540
Who has the communicator to the school?

00:23:37.540 --> 00:23:41.290
I did, but I think I dropped it.

00:23:41.290 --> 00:23:45.500
Then it's lost. Is there anywhere
we can evacuate to?

00:23:45.500 --> 00:23:47.200
Hmm?

00:23:47.200 --> 00:23:51.330
Is that a ship over there?

00:23:51.330 --> 00:23:52.700
What?!

00:23:52.700 --> 00:23:54.540
Is someone on board?

00:23:54.540 --> 00:23:58.410
Does everyone see it? Let's regroup there!

00:23:58.410 --> 00:24:00.200
Use your thrusters.

00:24:00.200 --> 00:24:04.700
It doesn't have much fuel, but there
should be enough to reach the ship.

00:24:12.160 --> 00:24:13.910
Looking for this?

00:24:17.500 --> 00:24:21.410
Guys, try to recover luggage
if you see any nearby.

00:24:31.790 --> 00:24:35.950
What's going on... Why is this happening?

00:24:36.790 --> 00:24:39.620
No response from the inside.

00:24:39.620 --> 00:24:41.410
It must be unoccupied.

00:24:49.250 --> 00:24:51.040
Power is online.

00:24:54.040 --> 00:24:57.080
Once everyone's inside, close the airlock!

00:24:58.200 --> 00:25:00.290
What about the gravity controls?

00:25:00.290 --> 00:25:01.910
I just activated them.

00:25:01.910 --> 00:25:05.250
Hey, what's going on? What is this?!

00:25:05.250 --> 00:25:07.700
Brace yourselves, gravity incoming!

00:25:12.250 --> 00:25:16.830
Looks like a locker room over there.
Let's gather there for now.

00:25:19.000 --> 00:25:20.410
What is going on?!

00:25:20.410 --> 00:25:22.200
What was that ball?!

00:25:22.200 --> 00:25:23.790
Calm down, Quitterie.

00:25:23.790 --> 00:25:26.370
First let's check if we're all safe.

00:25:26.370 --> 00:25:28.370
Are all nine of us here?

00:25:28.370 --> 00:25:30.200
Is anyone injured?

00:25:30.200 --> 00:25:31.080
Hey...

00:25:32.700 --> 00:25:34.660
We're missing one.

00:25:36.910 --> 00:25:38.080
Who?

00:25:39.450 --> 00:25:40.950
Who are we missing?!

00:25:43.410 --> 00:25:45.080
Isn't that her?

00:26:04.950 --> 00:26:07.620
I see her! That's...

00:26:07.620 --> 00:26:09.540
Aries!

00:26:09.540 --> 00:26:11.410
Her thrusters are disabled!

00:26:11.410 --> 00:26:13.660
Looks like her comms are down too.

00:26:13.660 --> 00:26:15.410
We have to go save her.

00:26:15.410 --> 00:26:21.620
She's too far. If we run out of fuel,
we won't be able to come back.

00:26:21.620 --> 00:26:22.950
No...

00:26:23.870 --> 00:26:25.750
It's hopeless then!

00:26:25.750 --> 00:26:28.330
What are we gonna do?!

00:26:28.330 --> 00:26:32.250
Shut up! Think of something!

00:26:37.410 --> 00:26:39.870
When things seem hopeless...

00:26:39.870 --> 00:26:41.290
...act tough!

00:26:55.290 --> 00:26:56.750
I'll go.

00:26:58.200 --> 00:27:02.450
I hate that word, "hopeless."

00:27:05.750 --> 00:27:07.120
Is it secure?

00:27:07.120 --> 00:27:08.080
Yeah.

00:27:08.080 --> 00:27:10.750
You should be able to make the one-way trip.

00:27:10.750 --> 00:27:13.120
We'll pull you back with the wire.

00:27:15.750 --> 00:27:17.330
I'm going now.

00:27:24.000 --> 00:27:25.660
How is it?

00:27:25.660 --> 00:27:27.660
A little off to the right.

00:27:27.660 --> 00:27:29.620
Kanata, you're off!

00:27:29.620 --> 00:27:31.410
Really? Which way?

00:27:31.410 --> 00:27:35.830
Right... Oh wait, she's moving too, so...

00:27:35.830 --> 00:27:38.500
Uh... Left? West?

00:27:38.500 --> 00:27:39.700
Which way?!

00:27:39.700 --> 00:27:44.450
Kanata, conserve your thruster fuel.
Minimize your bursts!

00:27:44.450 --> 00:27:47.580
One-point-five second burst, seven o'clock.

00:27:47.580 --> 00:27:50.700
Once you're on the trajectory,
let inertia take you there.

00:27:50.700 --> 00:27:53.000
Got it!

00:27:53.000 --> 00:27:54.830
You're on the trajectory.

00:27:56.870 --> 00:27:59.330
Hold on...

00:27:59.330 --> 00:28:00.700
Aries...!

00:28:06.910 --> 00:28:08.620
Everyone's gone...

00:28:10.700 --> 00:28:12.750
I'm scared...

00:28:14.750 --> 00:28:18.160
Being all alone is terrifying...!

00:28:29.700 --> 00:28:30.950
Kanata!

00:28:30.950 --> 00:28:34.160
Hey there, dizzy enough yet?

00:28:45.120 --> 00:28:47.120
There's not enough wire!

00:28:47.120 --> 00:28:48.830
No!

00:29:14.410 --> 00:29:19.080
Get to space, Kanata!

00:29:26.040 --> 00:29:29.120
If the rope won't reach her...

00:29:29.120 --> 00:29:30.790
What is he doing?

00:29:30.790 --> 00:29:32.580
I'll go myself!

00:29:36.540 --> 00:29:39.200
And... Yeah.

00:29:40.500 --> 00:29:42.910
Wow, this is scary.

00:29:42.910 --> 00:29:46.200
Darkness all around.

00:29:46.200 --> 00:29:49.580
I could easily drown in the fear.

00:29:49.580 --> 00:29:52.330
Nowhere to go but forward.

00:29:53.750 --> 00:29:57.330
Can you see me now, Teacher?

00:30:04.080 --> 00:30:06.330
Kanata! Kanata!

00:30:06.330 --> 00:30:08.750
You did well, Aries!

00:30:08.750 --> 00:30:10.660
Thank you...

00:30:10.660 --> 00:30:14.200
Hold on, don't let go.

00:30:17.080 --> 00:30:20.750
Yeah, you're saying "thank you," right?

00:30:22.120 --> 00:30:26.200
Okay, time for the hard part...

00:30:26.200 --> 00:30:27.790
Can they come back?

00:30:27.790 --> 00:30:30.500
The wire is far away now,

00:30:30.500 --> 00:30:34.790
but there should be enough fuel left
to drift back here with inertia.

00:30:44.500 --> 00:30:46.500
Just enough.

00:30:46.500 --> 00:30:49.540
Now, as long as I stay on course...

00:30:49.540 --> 00:30:51.500
No, you can't.

00:30:51.500 --> 00:30:55.870
Your trajectory is off,
five degrees downwards.

00:30:55.870 --> 00:30:58.580
You're going to fly past us.

00:30:58.580 --> 00:31:00.540
What can we do?!

00:31:00.540 --> 00:31:03.790
There's no more thruster fuel...

00:31:03.790 --> 00:31:07.580
Then there's nothing we can do...

00:31:19.410 --> 00:31:23.580
I want to be friends with everyone.

00:31:30.580 --> 00:31:31.750
I know!

00:31:31.750 --> 00:31:33.200
Hey!

00:31:33.200 --> 00:31:34.790
Lend me a hand!

00:31:46.830 --> 00:31:49.290
Am I out of reach again?!

00:31:55.660 --> 00:31:57.540
Kanata...!

00:31:57.540 --> 00:31:59.910
Kanata, look!

00:32:06.830 --> 00:32:07.910
Hey!

00:32:07.910 --> 00:32:09.830
Now we're even.

00:32:09.830 --> 00:32:11.290
Huh?

00:32:11.290 --> 00:32:12.580
Kanata!

00:32:28.080 --> 00:32:29.830
Hello, welcome home.

00:32:29.830 --> 00:32:31.700
That was crazy dangerous!

00:32:31.700 --> 00:32:32.910
Sorry!

00:32:32.910 --> 00:32:34.410
I...

00:32:39.000 --> 00:32:41.080
Are you saying something?

00:32:43.200 --> 00:32:46.410
I was so scared,

00:32:46.410 --> 00:32:48.450
but once you held my hand,

00:32:48.450 --> 00:32:51.290
space looks very beautiful.

00:32:51.290 --> 00:32:52.870
That's what I said.

00:33:01.160 --> 00:33:03.200
Thank you so much!

00:33:03.200 --> 00:33:05.160
Don't mention it.

00:33:05.160 --> 00:33:08.290
It's not your fault
that your suit was broken.

00:33:08.290 --> 00:33:11.080
You really can't be left alone, can you?

00:33:11.080 --> 00:33:13.410
I owe you all my life.

00:33:13.410 --> 00:33:19.620
It's fine. It's not like we took
a stupid risk like Kanata did.

00:33:21.790 --> 00:33:26.410
Anyway, it's too bad the communicator
is broken on this ship.

00:33:26.410 --> 00:33:28.700
We have to let the school know immediately.

00:33:28.700 --> 00:33:32.790
They should notice when we fail
to report in on schedule.

00:33:32.790 --> 00:33:36.040
What? So we have to sit and wait for help?

00:33:36.040 --> 00:33:40.250
McPa is only nine light years from home.
It'll only take them four hours.

00:33:40.250 --> 00:33:43.410
Come on, at least we're alive, right?

00:33:43.410 --> 00:33:45.950
Don't be so sure that help is coming.

00:33:47.080 --> 00:33:51.080
Look at that planet. I surveyed it.

00:33:51.080 --> 00:33:54.410
It's a lifeless, ice-covered planet.

00:33:56.950 --> 00:33:58.950
It's not McPa.

00:34:00.040 --> 00:34:02.830
We're not over McPa?!

00:34:02.830 --> 00:34:05.410
Currently, this ship is...

00:34:05.410 --> 00:34:08.500
...5,012 light years away.

00:34:08.500 --> 00:34:11.750
F-Five thousand twelve light years?!

00:34:11.750 --> 00:34:14.620
I don't understand how we can be.

00:34:14.620 --> 00:34:18.750
But... given how far we are,

00:34:18.750 --> 00:34:22.250
the chance of a rescue is close to none.

00:34:23.620 --> 00:34:28.540
Space camp log, Aries Spring, day one.

00:34:28.540 --> 00:34:32.700
We, team B5 of Caird High Planet Camp,

00:34:32.700 --> 00:34:37.500
are lost in the far reaches of space...

00:34:37.500 --> 00:34:40.500
Acting tough is getting really hard now...

00:34:43.870 --> 00:34:46.620
What's going on?

00:34:46.620 --> 00:34:49.120
What do you mean, 5,012 light years?!

00:34:49.120 --> 00:34:52.700
I don't understand how it happened.

00:34:52.700 --> 00:34:56.870
That sphere engulfed us, and spat us out
5,000 light years in deep space.

00:34:56.870 --> 00:35:00.910
Hey, so can we go back in the ball
and go back to where we were?

00:35:00.910 --> 00:35:02.500
You could be right!

00:35:02.500 --> 00:35:06.120
So where is that nice magic ball, then?

00:35:06.120 --> 00:35:09.000
Is it floating around in your head?

00:35:09.000 --> 00:35:11.910
Huh? Who asked you?

00:35:11.910 --> 00:35:13.330
Friends, please.

00:35:13.330 --> 00:35:19.330
It's true though, the ball isn't here.
We don't even know how to find it.

00:35:19.330 --> 00:35:21.700
Hmm, you could be right.

00:35:21.700 --> 00:35:23.500
Then... what do we do?

00:35:23.500 --> 00:35:25.080
Um.

00:35:25.080 --> 00:35:29.870
I'm thinking, maybe this is
like a test of some sort?

00:35:29.870 --> 00:35:31.370
A test?

00:35:31.370 --> 00:35:34.040
Think about it, it's all too weird.

00:35:34.040 --> 00:35:36.790
Five thousand light years in an instant?

00:35:36.790 --> 00:35:39.200
And we happen to appear next to a ship?

00:35:39.200 --> 00:35:46.160
Maybe the ship's computers are lying
and we're actually still over McPa.

00:35:46.160 --> 00:35:49.950
Maybe they're watching us to see
how we tackle the situation!

00:35:49.950 --> 00:35:52.290
That's it!

00:35:52.290 --> 00:35:54.700
That sounds like the best explanation!

00:35:54.700 --> 00:35:56.870
Yeah, it's all staged!

00:35:56.870 --> 00:35:58.500
You could be right!

00:35:58.500 --> 00:35:59.830
Our helmets...

00:35:59.830 --> 00:36:00.750
Huh?

00:36:00.750 --> 00:36:06.290
Kanata told us to put our helmets on.

00:36:06.290 --> 00:36:07.790
But...

00:36:07.790 --> 00:36:12.330
If we hadn't... we would have died, instantly.

00:36:13.330 --> 00:36:17.830
I don't think the school would
do something so dangerous.

00:36:18.830 --> 00:36:20.410
You could be right.

00:36:20.410 --> 00:36:23.950
How many times are you going
to say, "You could be right"?!

00:36:23.950 --> 00:36:30.410
If there's no way to fly this ship,
it might as well be a coffin.

00:36:35.290 --> 00:36:39.250
Hey, Zack! You have a spaceship
license, don't you?!

00:36:39.250 --> 00:36:42.410
Huh? A high school student? Seriously?

00:36:43.250 --> 00:36:44.080
Seriously.

00:36:44.080 --> 00:36:47.200
Then why didn't you say something?!

00:36:47.200 --> 00:36:48.450
I didn't want to.

00:36:48.450 --> 00:36:50.750
What's his deal?!

00:36:50.750 --> 00:36:54.200
Is he famous?

00:36:54.200 --> 00:36:55.700
You didn't know?

00:36:55.700 --> 00:36:59.200
He's Zack Walker,
super genius with a 200 IQ.

00:36:59.200 --> 00:37:02.790
No, we don't know. Why are you gloating?

00:37:02.790 --> 00:37:08.290
The ship is old, but it can fly using
propellant gathered from space vacuum.

00:37:08.290 --> 00:37:11.410
So we can get home!

00:37:14.700 --> 00:37:17.000
Everyone, calm down.

00:37:18.250 --> 00:37:22.160
To travel 5,000 light years, even with
maximum faster-than-light drive,

00:37:22.160 --> 00:37:24.290
it would take at least three months.

00:37:24.290 --> 00:37:27.700
Even with all of our baggage put together,
we only have enough food and water

00:37:27.700 --> 00:37:30.580
for three days of travel.

00:37:30.580 --> 00:37:33.540
What if we lighten the load of the ship?

00:37:33.540 --> 00:37:36.700
Can we disable a limiter and boost the engines?

00:37:36.700 --> 00:37:39.660
I've calculated all of that already.

00:37:39.660 --> 00:37:45.370
Even with full tanks, the ship can
only carry 20 days' worth of water.

00:37:45.370 --> 00:37:49.750
This ship... just isn't capable of
travelling 5,000 light years.

00:37:51.410 --> 00:37:54.250
So much impressive jargon...

00:37:54.250 --> 00:37:57.200
Just say it, it's hopeless.

00:37:57.200 --> 00:38:00.330
Even for a genius like you.

00:38:00.330 --> 00:38:02.370
So let's give up and die, right?

00:38:06.330 --> 00:38:08.290
Hey.

00:38:08.290 --> 00:38:10.950
Fighting won't help.

00:38:10.950 --> 00:38:13.870
Everyone, calm down, listen!

00:38:13.870 --> 00:38:16.000
"Those who panic are easily confused!"

00:38:18.290 --> 00:38:21.790
It's number three on my list of survival tips.

00:38:21.790 --> 00:38:23.540
What's he saying?

00:38:23.540 --> 00:38:26.540
You're just stating the obvious.

00:38:26.540 --> 00:38:30.080
Just listen to me for a bit.

00:38:30.080 --> 00:38:33.700
Why should we listen to you?

00:38:33.700 --> 00:38:38.950
When I was in middle school,
I went on a mountain climbing trip.

00:38:38.950 --> 00:38:41.950
We got lost there, just five students.

00:38:43.370 --> 00:38:47.370
Just students? What about the teacher?

00:38:50.450 --> 00:38:55.950
The unexpected storm,
broken communicator, landslide...

00:38:55.950 --> 00:39:01.410
A bunch of accidents happened at once,
and a student got into a panic and slipped.

00:39:01.410 --> 00:39:05.910
Our teacher tried to save him,
and fell down a ledge.

00:39:05.910 --> 00:39:07.540
He lost his life.

00:39:09.000 --> 00:39:15.120
The rest of us, just kids, survived
for seven days until help arrived.

00:39:16.250 --> 00:39:19.790
It was a miracle that none of us died.

00:39:19.790 --> 00:39:24.580
I've heard of that--
the Surugi Middle School Incident...

00:39:24.580 --> 00:39:27.040
You were part of it?

00:39:27.040 --> 00:39:32.700
We almost gave up, many times.
But we cheered each other up.

00:39:32.700 --> 00:39:36.200
I'm sure I would have died without them.

00:39:36.200 --> 00:39:38.700
We have to stick together.

00:39:41.040 --> 00:39:44.200
If we're surrounded by darkness...

00:39:44.200 --> 00:39:46.160
...we have to hold each other's hands.

00:39:48.160 --> 00:39:50.330
I understand!

00:39:50.330 --> 00:39:54.870
Out there, when I thought it was all over,

00:39:54.870 --> 00:39:58.330
you all held hands to save me.

00:40:00.620 --> 00:40:04.000
Right now, we're all separated.

00:40:04.000 --> 00:40:08.200
We don't even know each other's names.

00:40:08.200 --> 00:40:10.830
That's not right.

00:40:10.830 --> 00:40:13.500
So, let's go back and...

00:40:22.910 --> 00:40:26.870
Quitterie. Quitterie Rafaeli.

00:40:28.410 --> 00:40:33.040
Zack Walker. I'm studying
to become a researcher.

00:40:33.040 --> 00:40:38.160
Luca here. I'm good at making stuff.
Trying to get into an art school.

00:40:39.500 --> 00:40:43.540
Charce Lacroix. I guess I'm good at biology.

00:40:43.540 --> 00:40:44.790
And you?

00:40:44.790 --> 00:40:46.330
Huh?

00:40:46.330 --> 00:40:48.120
Introduction.

00:40:48.120 --> 00:40:52.500
Um, I... I'm Yunhua.

00:40:52.500 --> 00:40:55.160
I'm not good at anything, but...

00:40:55.160 --> 00:40:58.040
I... I'm sorry.

00:40:58.040 --> 00:41:01.120
Ha, ha, don't...

00:41:04.750 --> 00:41:07.120
...be sorry.

00:41:07.120 --> 00:41:09.410
He's good-looking, but his rhythm is weird!

00:41:09.410 --> 00:41:11.410
Come, dear.

00:41:11.410 --> 00:41:13.660
How is his face shining?!

00:41:13.660 --> 00:41:17.160
One day, you'll get your turn to shine.

00:41:17.160 --> 00:41:19.540
Even his words are shiny!

00:41:29.410 --> 00:41:32.910
I'm Funicia Rafaeli, the little sister.

00:41:41.540 --> 00:41:42.830
I'm Ulgar.

00:41:42.830 --> 00:41:44.950
Pleasure to meet ya!

00:41:44.950 --> 00:41:46.120
What is this?!

00:41:46.120 --> 00:41:48.330
I'm Beego, dude.

00:41:49.700 --> 00:41:51.790
It's just hand-holding, don't overreact.

00:41:51.790 --> 00:41:53.870
Encounter with the unknown.

00:41:55.290 --> 00:41:56.750
I know!

00:41:56.750 --> 00:42:00.410
Maybe if we connect it, we can make it!

00:42:00.410 --> 00:42:02.120
What do you mean?

00:42:02.120 --> 00:42:04.120
I understand!

00:42:04.120 --> 00:42:07.660
Even if we can't do it alone, together,
we could reach out.

00:42:07.660 --> 00:42:10.450
So we can all be stars!

00:42:10.450 --> 00:42:13.160
Where is she going with this?!

00:42:13.160 --> 00:42:16.500
Stars... You mean planets?

00:42:16.500 --> 00:42:17.750
Yes!

00:42:17.750 --> 00:42:19.700
Huh? What?

00:42:20.660 --> 00:42:27.620
If there's a planet within three days
from here, with food and water...

00:42:31.580 --> 00:42:37.000
...I can enter the conditions into
this list of planets I brought along.

00:42:37.000 --> 00:42:39.620
I found one.

00:42:39.620 --> 00:42:41.870
Planet Vilavurs.

00:42:42.620 --> 00:42:44.700
Three days from here.

00:42:44.700 --> 00:42:49.370
If we go to that planet and
stock up on food and water,

00:42:49.370 --> 00:42:51.200
we can fly for 20 more days.

00:42:51.200 --> 00:42:52.950
I see!

00:42:52.950 --> 00:42:58.620
Then, if we can find another planet
with food and water...

00:42:58.620 --> 00:43:02.250
Wait, seriously? Is this possible?

00:43:02.250 --> 00:43:06.410
And we keep connecting planets
that are 20 days apart or less...

00:43:06.410 --> 00:43:10.660
How many stars do we have to go to...?

00:43:14.080 --> 00:43:15.620
We can...

00:43:21.790 --> 00:43:25.700
Progress, little by little.

00:43:30.620 --> 00:43:32.250
I got it.

00:43:35.500 --> 00:43:40.410
There's just one route, spanning five planets.

00:43:42.500 --> 00:43:46.080
It's a miracle that such a route exists!

00:43:46.080 --> 00:43:48.790
Good job, Zack!

00:43:48.790 --> 00:43:51.200
You really think it's possible?

00:43:52.790 --> 00:43:54.830
I'd say 50/50.

00:43:54.830 --> 00:43:57.910
But it's either that or death.

00:43:57.910 --> 00:44:02.580
If there's a way, let's go on it.

00:44:02.580 --> 00:44:04.410
First tip of survival,
going forward results in progress!

00:44:04.410 --> 00:44:06.540
Stating the obvious again!

00:44:06.540 --> 00:44:08.830
Are you stupid?

00:44:08.830 --> 00:44:10.950
Let's move this ship.

00:44:10.950 --> 00:44:12.450
Yeah!

00:44:20.910 --> 00:44:25.080
Is everyone seated? Sit properly, okay?

00:44:25.080 --> 00:44:28.950
Please remain seated while the sign is on.

00:44:28.950 --> 00:44:32.540
We get it, so you sit, too.

00:44:32.540 --> 00:44:34.120
On the captain's seat.

00:44:34.120 --> 00:44:35.330
Huh?

00:44:36.660 --> 00:44:40.790
We do need a leader to stay together.

00:44:40.790 --> 00:44:44.000
Yes. And he volunteered, too.

00:44:44.000 --> 00:44:45.410
I agree!

00:44:45.410 --> 00:44:46.910
--Yes!
--Right on.

00:44:46.910 --> 00:44:49.790
I don't mind.

00:44:52.620 --> 00:44:55.750
--Oh, but I'm not ready to be captain!

00:44:55.750 --> 00:44:57.660
--Why the sudden change?!
--Oh, but I'm not ready to be captain!

00:44:57.660 --> 00:45:00.540
There aren't any more chairs. Just sit.

00:45:00.540 --> 00:45:03.660
Uh, okay.

00:45:03.660 --> 00:45:06.330
Okay, let's go...

00:45:06.330 --> 00:45:08.830
Set course. First planet, Vila--

00:45:08.830 --> 00:45:11.580
Does this ship have a name?

00:45:11.580 --> 00:45:13.750
Don't cut me off!

00:45:13.750 --> 00:45:17.000
Name, name of ship...

00:45:17.000 --> 00:45:20.000
Who cares if... Hmm?

00:45:20.000 --> 00:45:23.370
What's that? Written on that plate.

00:45:24.330 --> 00:45:27.580
"Per Aspera Ad Astra."

00:45:27.580 --> 00:45:29.870
What's that?

00:45:29.870 --> 00:45:33.160
Aspera means hardship. Astra means star.

00:45:33.160 --> 00:45:36.080
"Overcome hardships to reach your goal."

00:45:36.080 --> 00:45:40.620
That's nice. A lot better than
Kanata's dumb survival tips.

00:45:40.620 --> 00:45:42.750
What?!

00:45:42.750 --> 00:45:47.540
So it's an old word for "star"? That works.

00:45:47.540 --> 00:45:52.870
The ship's name is... <i>Astra</i>.

00:45:58.250 --> 00:46:02.450
Set course for the first planet, Vilavurs.

00:46:05.450 --> 00:46:08.410
Activate faster-than-light engines!
